== THM-486: the involution modulus 24 is the Pisano modulus ==
  pi(24) = 24 (= 24); pi(n)=n exactly for n in [1, 24, 120, 600, 3000] = {1} U {24*5^k} (Fulton-Morris)
  => 24 is the SMALLEST n>1 with pi(n)=n (the involution modulus is the base Pisano-fixed point)
  alpha(24) = 12 (rank of apparition); F_12 = 144 = 12^2 (unique nontrivial Fibonacci square)
  pi(p) | p^2-1 AND 24 | p^2-1 for primes 7..61: True  (same p^2-1, THM-484 link)

